{"step_index":858,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:29:08Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:29:08+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:29:08+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 1 to 537\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: /-\n2: GraphInvariantsComputable.lean — a *computable* mirror of the invariants in\n3: `GraphInvariants.lean`, so that a claim about one explicit finite graph can be\n4: settled by `decide` rather than by a hand proof.\n5: \n6: Why this file exists\n7: --------------------\n8: `GraphInvariants.lean` defines the invariants the way a mathematician states\n9: them: `dominationNumber G = sInf { n | ∃ s, s.card = n ∧ G.IsDominatingSet s }`.\n10: That is the right *specification*, but `sInf` over a `Set ℕ` (under\n11: `open scoped Classical`) is **noncomputable**, so the kernel cannot evaluate it\n12: on a concrete graph — measured directly, `decide` succeeds on `order`, `size`\n13: and `minDegree`, and fails on every `sInf`/`sSup` invariant (domination,\n14: annihilation, the zero-forcing family, and mathlib's own `indepNum`/`cliqueNum`).\n15: \n16: That blocks the cheapest source of formal results we have. The refutation engine\n17: kills thousands of candidates and knows exactly which graph kills each one; each\n18: such pair is a `¬∀ …` theorem whose proof is \"evaluate both sides on this graph\"\n19: — but only if the invariants actually evaluate.\n20: \n21: The definitions here are the same mathematical objects expressed as a minimum\n22: over an explicitly enumerated `Finset`, which the kernel *can* reduce. They are\n23: deliberately kept in their own namespace: nothing in the existing proof pipeline\n24: changes, and `GraphInvariants.lean` remains the specification of record.\n25: -/\n26: import Mathlib\n27: \n28: open Finset\n29: \n30: namespace GraphCalc\n31: \n32: variable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n33: \n34: /-- Least cardinality of a subset satisfying `p`, or `0` when none does.\n35: \n36: The `0` fallback is only harmless when *some* subset satisfies `p` — for\n37: `indepNum`, `dominationNumber` and `vertexCoverNumber`, `univ` always does. It\n38: is NOT harmless in general, and treating it as such produced a real defect:\n39: `IsConnectedZeroForcingSet` is unsatisfiable on a disconnected graph (`univ`\n40: does not induce a connected subgraph), so the invariant silently read `0` where\n41: graphcalc reports \"undefined\". A conjecture `Z_c + 2 ≤ 2 * Z_t` then became\n42: `2 ≤ 0` and was refutable with no mathematical content.\n43: \n44: Any new invariant built on `minCard` must either prove `univ` satisfies its\n45: predicate, or expose a `Has…` witness predicate below and be exported under it. -/\n46: def minCard (p : Finset V → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n47:   ((univ.powerset.filter p).image Finset.card).min.getD 0\n48: \n49: /-- Some subset satisfies `p`: exactly the precondition `minCard` needs for its\n50: value to mean \"the least cardinality\" rather than \"there were none\". -/\n51: def HasWitness (p : Finset V → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : Prop :=\n52:   ∃ s ∈ (univ : Finset V).powerset, p s\n53: \n54: instance (p : Finset V → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : Decidable (HasWitness p) := by\n55:   unfold HasWitness; infer_instance\n56: \n57: /-- Greatest `k ≤ n` satisfying `p`, or `0` when none does. -/\n58: def maxUpTo (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n59:   (((range (n + 1)).filter p).max).getD 0\n60: \n61: /-- Least `k ≤ n` satisfying `p`, or `n` when none does. -/\n62: def minUpTo (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n63:   (((range (n + 1)).filter p).min).getD n\n64: \n65: /- ── order / size ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n66: \n67: def order (_G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ := Fintype.card V\n68: \n69: def size (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ := G.edgeFinset.card\n70: \n71: /- ── independence / clique ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n72: \n73: /-- `s` is independent: no two of its vertices are adjacent. -/\n74: def IsIndependentFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n75:   ∀ u ∈ s, ∀ w ∈ s, ¬ G.Adj u w\n76: \n77: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n78:     Decidable (IsIndependentFinset G s) := by\n79:   unfold IsIndependentFinset; infer_instance\n80: \n81: /-- Independence number: the largest independent set. -/\n82: def indepNum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n83:   (((univ.powerset.filter (IsIndependentFinset G)).image Finset.card).max).getD 0\n84: \n85: /-- `s` is a clique: distinct vertices of `s` are pairwise adjacent. -/\n86: def IsCliqueFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n87:   ∀ u ∈ s, ∀ w ∈ s, u ≠ w → G.Adj u w\n88: \n89: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n90:     Decidable (IsCliqueFinset G s) := by\n91:   unfold IsCliqueFinset; infer_instance\n92: \n93: /-- Clique number: the largest clique. -/\n94: def cliqueNum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n95:   (((univ.powerset.filter (IsCliqueFinset G)).image Finset.card).max).getD 0\n96: \n97: /- ── domination family ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n98: \n99: def IsDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n100:   ∀ v : V, v ∈ s ∨ ∃ w ∈ s, G.Adj v w\n101: \n102: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n103:     Decidable (IsDominatingSet G s) := by\n104:   unfold IsDominatingSet; infer_instance\n105: \n106: def dominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n107:   minCard (IsDominatingSet G)\n108: \n109: def IsIndependentDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n110:     (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n111:   IsDominatingSet G s ∧ IsIndependentFinset G s\n112: \n113: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n114:     Decidable (IsIndependentDominatingSet G s) := by\n115:   unfold IsIndependentDominatingSet; infer_instance\n116: \n117: def independentDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n118:   minCard (IsIndependentDominatingSet G)\n119: \n120: /- ── degree-sequence invariants ───────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n121: \n122: /-- Sum of the `k` smallest degrees.\n123: \n124: Stated as a minimum over `k`-element subsets rather than by sorting the degree\n125: sequence: the two agree (a `k`-subset of minimum degree-sum is exactly a choice\n126: of `k` smallest degrees), and this form stays decidable, whereas both\n127: `Multiset.sort` and `Finset.toList` are noncomputable and stall kernel\n128: reduction. -/\n129: def smallestDegreeSum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) : ℕ :=\n130:   (((univ.powersetCard k).image (fun s => ∑ v ∈ s, G.degree v)).min).getD 0\n131: \n132: /-- Sum of the `k` largest degrees (dual of `smallestDegreeSum`). -/\n133: def largestDegreeSum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) : ℕ :=\n134:   (((univ.powersetCard k).image (fun s => ∑ v ∈ s, G.degree v)).max).getD 0\n135: \n136: /-- Annihilation number: largest `k` whose `k` smallest degrees sum to `≤ m`. -/\n137: def annihilationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n138:   maxUpTo (Fintype.card V) (fun k => smallestDegreeSum G k ≤ size G)\n139: \n140: /-- Slater number: least `t` with `t +` (sum of the `t` largest degrees) `≥ n`. -/\n141: def slaterNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n142:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V)\n143:     (fun t => Fintype.card V ≤ t + largestDegreeSum G t)\n144: \n145: /- ── bipartite ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n146: \n147: /-- `G` is bipartite: some vertex set has every edge crossing it.\n148: \n149: The specification says `G.Colorable 2`, which quantifies over colourings and has\n150: no `Decidable` instance, so `decide` cannot touch it — leaving `bipartite` a\n151: class that could be *stated* in an exported theorem but never refuted on a\n152: witness. Searching the powerset is decidable and finite; `isBipartiteClass_iff`\n153: proves the two agree. -/\n154: def IsBipartiteClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n155:   ∃ s ∈ (univ : Finset V).powerset,\n156:     ∀ u ∈ (univ : Finset V), ∀ v ∈ (univ : Finset V), G.Adj u v → (u ∈ s ↔ v ∉ s)\n157: \n158: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n159:     Decidable (IsBipartiteClass G) := by\n160:   unfold IsBipartiteClass; infer_instance\n161: \n162: /- ── vertex cover ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n163: \n164: /-- `s` covers every edge. This is mathlib's `SimpleGraph.IsVertexCover`\n165: restricted to a `Finset`, which is what makes it decidable: mathlib quantifies\n166: over `Set V` and its `vertexCoverNum` is an `⨅` over that, hence noncomputable.\n167: `isVertexCoverFinset_iff` below proves the two agree, so the mathlib definition\n168: remains the specification and nothing is taken on trust. -/\n169: def IsVertexCoverFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n170:     Prop :=\n171:   ∀ u ∈ (univ : Finset V), ∀ v ∈ (univ : Finset V), G.Adj u v → u ∈ s ∨ v ∈ s\n172: \n173: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n174:     Decidable (IsVertexCoverFinset G s) := by\n175:   unfold IsVertexCoverFinset; infer_instance\n176: \n177: theorem isVertexCoverFinset_iff (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n178:     (s : Finset V) : IsVertexCoverFinset G s ↔ G.IsVertexCover (↑s : Set V) := by\n179:   simp [IsVertexCoverFinset, SimpleGraph.IsVertexCover]\n180: \n181: def vertexCoverNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n182:   minCard (IsVertexCoverFinset G)\n183: \n184: /- ── zero-forcing family ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n185: \n186: def forcingStep (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n187:   S ∪ univ.filter (fun w => w ∉ S ∧ ∃ v ∈ S, G.neighborFinset v \\ S = {w})\n188: \n189: def forcingClosure (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n190:   (forcingStep G)^[Fintype.card V] S\n191: \n192: def IsZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n193:   forcingClosure G S = univ\n194: \n195: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n196:     Decidable (IsZeroForcingSet G S) := by\n197:   unfold IsZeroForcingSet; infer_instance\n198: \n199: def zeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n200:   minCard (IsZeroForcingSet G)\n201: \n202: def IsTotalZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n203:   IsZeroForcingSet G S ∧ ∀ v ∈ S, ∃ w ∈ S, G.Adj v w\n204: \n205: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n206:     Decidable (IsTotalZeroForcingSet G S) := by\n207:   unfold IsTotalZeroForcingSet; infer_instance\n208: \n209: def totalZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n210:   minCard (IsTotalZeroForcingSet G)\n211: \n212: /-- `totalZeroForcingNumber` is meaningful: a total zero-forcing set exists.\n213: False whenever some vertex has no neighbour in any forcing set — isolated\n214: vertices being the common case. -/\n215: def HasTotalZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n216:   HasWitness (IsTotalZeroForcingSet G)\n217: \n218: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n219:     Decidable (HasTotalZeroForcingNumber G) := by\n220:   unfold HasTotalZeroForcingNumber; infer_instance\n221: \n222: /-- One step of reachability inside `S`: everything already in `T`, plus the\n223: vertices of `S` adjacent to it. -/\n224: def reachWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S T : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n225:   T ∪ S.filter (fun w => ∃ v ∈ T, G.Adj v w)\n226: \n227: /-- The vertices of `S` reachable from `v` without leaving `S`. Iterating `n`\n228: times suffices: each step that changes anything adds at least one vertex. -/\n229: def componentWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) (v : V) :\n230:     Finset V :=\n231:   (reachWithin G S)^[Fintype.card V] {v}\n232: \n233: /-- `S` induces a connected subgraph.\n234: \n235: The specification layer says `(G.induce ↑S).Connected`, which is a statement\n236: about walks in a subtype and carries no `Decidable` instance. This is the\n237: decidable equivalent: `S` is nonempty and every vertex of it reaches all of `S`\n238: from inside. `Connected` is `Preconnected ∧ Nonempty`, so both conjuncts are\n239: accounted for — the nonemptiness is not incidental. -/\n240: def IsConnectedSubset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n241:   S.Nonempty ∧ ∀ v ∈ S, componentWithin G S v = S\n242: \n243: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n244:     Decidable (IsConnectedSubset G S) := by\n245:   unfold IsConnectedSubset; infer_instance\n246: \n247: /-- A connected zero-forcing set: zero-forcing and inducing a connected\n248: subgraph, matching graphcalc's `is_connected_zero_forcing_set`. -/\n249: def IsConnectedZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n250:     Prop :=\n251:   IsZeroForcingSet G S ∧ IsConnectedSubset G S\n252: \n253: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) :\n254:     Decidable (IsConnectedZeroForcingSet G S) := by\n255:   unfold IsConnectedZeroForcingSet; infer_instance\n256: \n257: def connectedZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n258:   minCard (IsConnectedZeroForcingSet G)\n259: \n260: /-- `connectedZeroForcingNumber` is meaningful: a connected zero-forcing set\n261: exists. False on every disconnected graph, which is precisely where graphcalc\n262: reports no value and where the conjectures never made a claim. -/\n263: def HasConnectedZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n264:   HasWitness (IsConnectedZeroForcingSet G)\n265: \n266: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n267:     Decidable (HasConnectedZeroForcingNumber G) := by\n268:   unfold HasConnectedZeroForcingNumber; infer_instance\n269: \n270: /- ── graph-class predicates ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n271: \n272: def IsNontrivialClass (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := 2 ≤ order G\n273: \n274: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) : Decidable (IsNontrivialClass G) := by\n275:   unfold IsNontrivialClass; infer_instance\n276: \n277: def IsRegularClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n278:   ∀ u v : V, G.degree u = G.degree v\n279: \n280: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n281:     Decidable (IsRegularClass G) := by unfold IsRegularClass; infer_instance\n282: \n283: def IsCubicClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n284:   ∀ v : V, G.degree v = 3\n285: \n286: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n287:     Decidable (IsCubicClass G) := by unfold IsCubicClass; infer_instance\n288: \n289: def IsSubcubicClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n290:   ∀ v : V, G.degree v ≤ 3\n291: \n292: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n293:     Decidable (IsSubcubicClass G) := by unfold IsSubcubicClass; infer_instance\n294: \n295: /-- Eulerian: connected, with every degree even (graphcalc's `eulerian` is\n296: `networkx.is_eulerian`, which requires connectivity — see GraphInvariants). -/\n297: def IsEulerianClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n298:   G.Connected ∧ ∀ v : V, G.degree v % 2 = 0\n299: \n300: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n301:     Decidable (IsEulerianClass G) := by unfold IsEulerianClass; infer_instance\n302: \n303: /-- Triangle-free: no 3-element clique. -/\n304: def IsTriangleFreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n305:   ∀ s ∈ univ.powerset, IsCliqueFinset G s → s.card ≠ 3\n306: \n307: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n308:     Decidable (IsTriangleFreeClass G) := by\n309:   unfold IsTriangleFreeClass; infer_instance\n310: \n311: /-- `K₄`-free: no 4-element clique. -/\n312: def IsK4FreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n313:   ∀ s ∈ univ.powerset, IsCliqueFinset G s → s.card ≠ 4\n314: \n315: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n316:     Decidable (IsK4FreeClass G) := by unfold IsK4FreeClass; infer_instance\n317: \n318: /-- Connected. Mathlib's `SimpleGraph.Connected` already has a `Decidable`\n319: instance on a finite vertex type (`Connectivity/Finite.lean`) and it *does*\n320: reduce in the kernel — verified directly — so this is a plain alias rather than\n321: a reimplementation. -/\n322: def IsConnectedClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop := G.Connected\n323: \n324: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n325:     Decidable (IsConnectedClass G) := by unfold IsConnectedClass; infer_instance\n326: \n327: /-- A tree: connected with `m + 1 = n`.\n328: \n329: Mathlib's `SimpleGraph.IsTree` is built on `IsAcyclic`, a statement about *all*\n330: walks, and has no `Decidable` instance — `decide` fails on it outright. The edge\n331: count is the decidable equivalent, and `isTreeClass_iff` below proves the two\n332: agree, so nothing is taken on trust. -/\n333: def IsTreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n334:   G.Connected ∧ size G + 1 = order G\n335: \n336: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n337:     Decidable (IsTreeClass G) := by unfold IsTreeClass; infer_instance\n338: \n339: omit [DecidableEq V] in\n340: /-- The computable tree test is exactly mathlib's `IsTree`. -/\n341: theorem isTreeClass_iff (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n342:     IsTreeClass G ↔ G.IsTree := by\n343:   rw [SimpleGraph.isTree_iff_connected_and_card]\n344:   simp [IsTreeClass, size, order, Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Set.toFinset_card,\n345:         SimpleGraph.edgeFinset]\n346: \n347: /-- Claw-free: no vertex has three pairwise non-adjacent neighbours.\n348: \n349: Phrased through `IsIndependentFinset` over `powersetCard 3` rather than as four\n350: plain `∀ v a b c : V` binders with `a ≠ b` side conditions: the latter is the\n351: more readable statement (and is what `GraphInvariants.lean` records) but its\n352: `Decidable` instance does not reduce, so `decide` gets stuck on it. This form\n353: reduces. -/\n354: def IsClawFreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n355:   ∀ v ∈ (univ : Finset V), ∀ s ∈ univ.powersetCard 3,\n356:     (∀ u ∈ s, G.Adj v u) → ¬ IsIndependentFinset G s\n357: \n358: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n359:     Decidable (IsClawFreeClass G) := by unfold IsClawFreeClass; infer_instance\n360: \n361: /-- Cograph: no four vertices induce a path `P₄`. -/\n362: def IsCographClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n363:   ∀ a b c d : V, G.Adj a b → G.Adj b c → G.Adj c d →\n364:     ¬ G.Adj a c → ¬ G.Adj b d → G.Adj a d\n365: \n366: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n367:     Decidable (IsCographClass G) := by unfold IsCographClass; infer_instance\n368: \n369: /- ── sub-total domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n370: \n371: /-- Sub-total domination number: least `t` whose `t` largest degrees sum to\n372: `≥ n`.\n373: \n374: graphcalc computes this by sorting the degree sequence and scanning prefixes;\n375: `largestDegreeSum` is that prefix sum expressed as a maximum over `t`-subsets\n376: (see the note there on why sorting is not available to the kernel). -/\n377: def subTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n378:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V) (fun t => Fintype.card V ≤ largestDegreeSum G t)\n379: \n380: /-- Defined exactly when *some* prefix reaches `n`. graphcalc returns no value\n381: when the scan runs off the end — an edgeless graph has every degree `0`, so no\n382: prefix ever reaches `n` — while `minUpTo` would fall back to `n`. Monotonicity\n383: of `largestDegreeSum` makes the whole-graph check `t = n` sufficient. -/\n384: def HasSubTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n385:   Fintype.card V ≤ largestDegreeSum G (Fintype.card V)\n386: \n387: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n388:     Decidable (HasSubTotalDominationNumber G) := by\n389:   unfold HasSubTotalDominationNumber; infer_instance\n390: \n391: /- ── total domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n392: \n393: /-- Every vertex has a neighbour in `s` — note `G.Adj v u` excludes `v = u`, so\n394: a vertex may not dominate itself. -/\n395: def IsTotalDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n396:     Prop := ∀ v : V, ∃ u ∈ s, G.Adj v u\n397: \n398: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n399:     Decidable (IsTotalDominatingSet G s) := by\n400:   unfold IsTotalDominatingSet; infer_instance\n401: \n402: def totalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n403:   minCard (IsTotalDominatingSet G)\n404: \n405: /-- Undefined on a graph with an isolated vertex: nothing dominates it, so not\n406: even `univ` is a total dominating set and `minCard` would read `0`. graphcalc\n407: raises there rather than returning a number. -/\n408: def HasTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n409:   HasWitness (IsTotalDominatingSet G)\n410: \n411: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n412:     Decidable (HasTotalDominationNumber G) := by\n413:   unfold HasTotalDominationNumber; infer_instance\n414: \n415: /- ── edge cover ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n416: \n417: /-- A set of edges meeting every vertex. -/\n418: def IsEdgeCoverFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n419:     (s : Finset (Sym2 V)) : Prop := ∀ v : V, ∃ e ∈ s, v ∈ e\n420: \n421: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset (Sym2 V)) :\n422:     Decidable (IsEdgeCoverFinset G s) := by\n423:   unfold IsEdgeCoverFinset; infer_instance\n424: \n425: /-- Edge cover number: least `k ≤ n` such that some `k` edges meet every vertex.\n426: \n427: Searched by size over `edgeFinset`, not over its whole powerset. A minimum edge\n428: cover never needs more than `n - 1` edges (Gallai: `ρ = n − ν`, and `ν ≥ 1` once\n429: there is an edge), so bounding `k` by `n` loses nothing. It matters: the full\n430: powerset of `K₆`'s 15 edges is 32,768 subsets and exhausted the kernel's\n431: recursion depth, while the subsets of size at most 6 number 9,949. -/\n432: def edgeCoverNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n433:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V)\n434:     (fun k => ∃ s ∈ G.edgeFinset.powersetCard k, IsEdgeCoverFinset G s)\n435: \n436: /-- Undefined exactly when some vertex is isolated — networkx raises \"no edge\n437: cover exists\" there, and `minUpTo`'s fallback would read `n`. An edge cover\n438: exists iff every vertex has a neighbour (take one incident edge per vertex), so\n439: this is stated directly instead of by a second subset search. -/\n440: def HasEdgeCover (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n441:   ∀ v : V, ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u\n442: \n443: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n444:     Decidable (HasEdgeCover G) := by unfold HasEdgeCover; infer_instance\n445: \n446: /- ── Roman domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n447: \n448: /-- `f : V → {0,1,2}` is a Roman dominating function when every vertex labelled\n449: `0` has a neighbour labelled `2`.\n450: \n451: graphcalc solves this as a MIP over binaries `x, y` with `f = x + 2y`,\n452: constraint `x v + y v + Σ_{u ∈ N(v)} y u ≥ 1` and exclusion `x v + y v ≤ 1`;\n453: that is exactly the condition below. -/\n454: def IsRomanDominatingFunction (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n455:     (f : V → Fin 3) : Prop := ∀ v : V, f v = 0 → ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ f u = 2\n456: \n457: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (f : V → Fin 3) :\n458:     Decidable (IsRomanDominatingFunction G f) := by\n459:   unfold IsRomanDominatingFunction; infer_instance\n460: \n461: def romanWeight (f : V → Fin 3) : ℕ := ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ)\n462: \n463: /-- Total, not partial: the constant function `2` is always Roman dominating\n464: (no vertex is labelled `0`), so a witness always exists. -/\n465: def romanDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n466:   (((univ.filter (IsRomanDominatingFunction G)).image romanWeight).min).getD 0\n467: \n468: /- ── double Roman domination ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n469: \n470: /-- `f : V → {0,1,2,3}` is double Roman dominating when a vertex labelled `0`\n471: has either a neighbour labelled `3` or two neighbours labelled `2`, and a vertex\n472: labelled `1` has a neighbour labelled `≥ 2`.\n473: \n474: The first clause is written as graphcalc's linearisation\n475: `0.5·|N₂(v)| + |N₃(v)| ≥ 1`, but as two existentials rather than as\n476: `Finset.card` of a filter: \"at least two neighbours labelled 2\" is \"two distinct\n477: neighbours labelled 2\", and the kernel reduces a pair of quantifiers over `V`\n478: far more cheaply than it builds and counts a `Finset`. Written the counting way\n479: first, all seven order-5 checks exhausted their heartbeat budget. -/\n480: def IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n481:     (f : V → Fin 4) : Prop :=\n482:   (∀ v : V, f v = 0 →\n483:       (∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ f u = 3) ∨\n484:       (∃ u : V, ∃ w : V, u ≠ w ∧ G.Adj v u ∧ G.Adj v w ∧ f u = 2 ∧ f w = 2)) ∧\n485:   (∀ v : V, f v = 1 → ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ 2 ≤ (f u : ℕ))\n486: \n487: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (f : V → Fin 4) :\n488:     Decidable (IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction G f) := by\n489:   unfold IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction; infer_instance\n490: \n491: def doubleRomanWeight (f : V → Fin 4) : ℕ := ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ)\n492: \n493: /-- Total, for the same reason as `romanDominationNumber`: constant `3` works. -/\n494: def doubleRomanDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n495:   (((univ.filter (IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction G)).image\n496:     doubleRomanWeight).min).getD 0\n497: \n498: /- ── radius ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n499: \n500: /-- Vertices within `k` steps of `v`, by iterated neighbourhood expansion.\n501: Distance is not available to the kernel directly (`SimpleGraph.dist` is defined\n502: through `sInf` over walk lengths), so it is reconstructed as reachability. -/\n503: def ballWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ → V → Finset V\n504:   | 0,       v => {v}\n505:   | (k + 1), v =>\n506:       let B := ballWithin G k v\n507:       B ∪ B.biUnion (fun u => univ.filter (fun w => G.Adj u w))\n508: \n509: /-- Eccentricity of `v`: least `k` with every vertex within `k` steps. -/\n510: def eccentricity (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) : ℕ :=\n511:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V) (fun k => ballWithin G k v = univ)\n512: \n513: def radius (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n514:   ((univ.image (eccentricity G)).min).getD 0\n515: \n516: /-- Undefined on a disconnected graph, where some vertex never reaches all of\n517: `univ` and `minUpTo` would fall back to `n`. networkx raises there. -/\n518: def HasRadius (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n519:   ∀ v : V, ballWithin G (Fintype.card V) v = univ\n520: \n521: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n522:     Decidable (HasRadius G) := by unfold HasRadius; infer_instance\n523: \n524: /- ── graph construction from an explicit edge list ────────────────────────── -/\n525: \n526: /-- The graph on `Fin n` with the given edge list, symmetrised and loop-free.\n527: This is the shape the disproof exporter emits for a refuting witness.\n528: \n529: `SimpleGraph.fromRel` supplies the symmetry and irreflexivity proofs, so this\n530: stays a definition rather than a bundle of obligations that would have to be\n531: re-discharged (and re-adjusted across mathlib versions) in generated code. It is\n532: an `abbrev` so that `DecidableRel` synthesis can see through it at the use site. -/\n533: abbrev ofEdges (n : ℕ) (es : List (Fin n × Fin n)) : SimpleGraph (Fin n) :=\n534:   SimpleGraph.fromRel (fun u v => (u, v) ∈ es)\n535: \n536: end GraphCalc\n537: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
